        {
          "name": "run_acceptance",
          "canonical_hash": "sha256:2855e2e231d9a762f02367e5340e66578b0e232b72f4b7916e9051fd97773e2f",
          "description": "Evaluate the loaded AcceptanceSpec against live silicon state and return a deterministic pass/fail/error verdict per check (the closed-loop judge). An unreadable target is reported as 'error', never a silent pass. A failing/errored check derived by synthesize_acceptance carries provenance.source — the init function + line that should satisfy it — so fixes are precision-guided. Run load_acceptance first; halt the target at the state you want to assert.",
